{"type":"message","id":"f9ad1c50","parentId":"718c8250","timestamp":"2026-05-26T07:47:02.073Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"exec_ts_ZTI0ODMwYTctNWNkNi00MmZlLTk5OGItZWU1MzllNzJiOWMz","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"trafilatura -u \"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/26/ondo-finance-founder-nathan-allman-passes-away\" --output-format markdown > /tmp/coindesk_ondo.md\ntrafilatura -u \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/ondo-finance-founder-nathan-allman-passes-away-aged-32\" --output-format markdown > /tmp/cointelegraph_ondo.md\ncat /tmp/coindesk_ondo.md\ncat /tmp/cointelegraph_ondo.md\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":5566,"output":153,"cacheRead":9530,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15249,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779781619496,"responseId":"9E8Vatz6O6rs694PlvzqmQI"}}
{"type":"message","id":"4ab6fa2e","parentId":"f9ad1c50","timestamp":"2026-05-26T07:47:07.981Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"exec_ts_ZTI0ODMwYTctNWNkNi00MmZlLTk5OGItZWU1MzllNzJiOWMz","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Ondo Finance founder Nathan Allman dies unexpectedly\n\n## Tokenized real-world assets firm Ondo Finance announced the unexpected death of founder Nathan Allman on Tuesday, with longtime president Ian De Bode stepping in as CEO.\n\n#### What to know:\n\n- Ondo Finance said its founder, Nathan Allman, has died unexpectedly, without disclosing the cause of death.\n- Ian De Bode, the firm’s longtime president who has overseen strategy, product and daily operations, will become chief executive with the backing of the leadership team.\n- Allman, a Brown graduate and former member of Goldman Sachs’s digital assets team, founded Ondo in 2021 and led its growth into a tokenized real-world asset pioneer with $3.5 billion in total value locked and products including the USDY stablecoin and OUSG Treasury fund.\n\nOndo Finance founder Nathan Allman has died, the company said in a post on X on Tuesday, without disclosing the cause.\n\n\"It is with profound sadness that we announce the unexpected passing of Nathan Allman, Ondo's founder. Our hearts are with his family and loved ones,\" the company said. \"Nate's brilliance, humility, and drive shaped every part of what Ondo is today. His belief in the power of technology to create a more open, accessible financial system lives on in everything we build.\"\n\nIan De Bode, Ondo's longtime president who has led strategy, product, and day-to-day operations for over two years, will serve as CEO. De Bode has the full confidence of the leadership team, the company said.\n\nAllman, a Brown University graduate, founded Ondo in 2021 after working on Goldman Sachs' digital assets team. Under his leadership, Ondo became a pioneer in tokenized real-world assets, growing total value locked to $3.5 billion.\n\nMajor products launched during his tenure include USDY, a yield-bearing stablecoin, OUSG, a tokenized U.S. Treasury fund, and tokenized equities through Ondo Global Markets.\n\nThe company said it would continue building what Allman started as the most meaningful way to honor him.\n\n**UPDATE (May 26, 7:17 UTC): **Changes headline wording.\n\nMore For You\n\nThe decentralized exchange’s new HIP-4 product lets traders bet on offchain events like inflation and interest-rate decisions, using validators rather than UMA-style external dispute resolution.\n\nWhat to know:\n\n- Hyperliquid has expanded its HIP-4 outcome market to let users trade prediction-style contracts on offchain events like U.S. inflation data and Federal Reserve decisions alongside crypto derivatives.\n- Unlike rival Polymarket, which relies on UMA’s external oracle, Hyperliquid resolves these markets through its own validator set, which ingests news, decides which...\nThe tokenization movement that Allman contributed to by founding Ondo in 2021 helped capture the attention of Wall Street giants such as BlackRock, who see potential in the technology to make trading and settlement more efficient.\n\nAllman previously worked in Goldman Sachs’ digital asset team prior to founding Ondo. Before that, he founded the crypto hedge fund ChainStreet Capital, which focused on algorithmic, event-driven trading.\n\nOndo said that the company’s president, Ian De Bode, would serve as CEO.\n\n“It’s been an incredibly sad day for Ondo Finance,” De Bode told Cointelegraph. “Nate was not only an incredible founder and visionary, but also a very close personal friend. He will be missed dearly.”\n\n“The mission of Ondo, Nate's mission, has not changed,” he added. “If Nate were here, he would want to continue executing with excellence. We will make him proud.”\n\nOndo vice president and head of marketing, Ben Grossman, said Allman “was a once-in-a-generation founder and visionary. He was absolutely brilliant, with a vision and drive that shaped the industry and everyone around him. He will be enormously missed.”\n\nOndo did not share further details on Allman’s death. An Ondo spokesperson said that Allman’s family has requested privacy at this time.\n\nMore on the subject"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":5839,"aggregated":"# Ondo Finance founder Nathan Allman dies unexpectedly\n\n## Tokenized real-world assets firm Ondo Finance announced the unexpected death of founder Nathan Allman on Tuesday, with longtime president Ian De Bode stepping in as CEO.\n\n#### What to know:\n\n- Ondo Finance said its founder, Nathan Allman, has died unexpectedly, without disclosing the cause of death.\n- Ian De Bode, the firm’s longtime president who has overseen strategy, product and daily operations, will become chief executive with the backing of the leadership team.\n- Allman, a Brown graduate and former member of Goldman Sachs’s digital assets team, founded Ondo in 2021 and led its growth into a tokenized real-world asset pioneer with $3.5 billion in total value locked and products including the USDY stablecoin and OUSG Treasury fund.\n\nOndo Finance founder Nathan Allman has died, the company said in a post on X on Tuesday, without disclosing the cause.\n\n\"It is with profound sadness that we announce the unexpected passing of Nathan Allman, Ondo's founder. Our hearts are with his family and loved ones,\" the company said. \"Nate's brilliance, humility, and drive shaped every part of what Ondo is today. His belief in the power of technology to create a more open, accessible financial system lives on in everything we build.\"\n\nIan De Bode, Ondo's longtime president who has led strategy, product, and day-to-day operations for over two years, will serve as CEO. De Bode has the full confidence of the leadership team, the company said.\n\nAllman, a Brown University graduate, founded Ondo in 2021 after working on Goldman Sachs' digital assets team. Under his leadership, Ondo became a pioneer in tokenized real-world assets, growing total value locked to $3.5 billion.\n\nMajor products launched during his tenure include USDY, a yield-bearing stablecoin, OUSG, a tokenized U.S. Treasury fund, and tokenized equities through Ondo Global Markets.\n\nThe company said it would continue building what Allman started as the most meaningful way to honor him.\n\n**UPDATE (May 26, 7:17 UTC): **Changes headline wording.\n\nMore For You\n\nThe decentralized exchange’s new HIP-4 product lets traders bet on offchain events like inflation and interest-rate decisions, using validators rather than UMA-style external dispute resolution.\n\nWhat to know:\n\n- Hyperliquid has expanded its HIP-4 outcome market to let users trade prediction-style contracts on offchain events like U.S. inflation data and Federal Reserve decisions alongside crypto derivatives.\n- Unlike rival Polymarket, which relies on UMA’s external oracle, Hyperliquid resolves these markets through its own validator set, which ingests news, decides which...\nThe tokenization movement that Allman contributed to by founding Ondo in 2021 helped capture the attention of Wall Street giants such as BlackRock, who see potential in the technology to make trading and settlement more efficient.\n\nAllman previously worked in Goldman Sachs’ digital asset team prior to founding Ondo. Before that, he founded the crypto hedge fund ChainStreet Capital, which focused on algorithmic, event-driven trading.\n\nOndo said that the company’s president, Ian De Bode, would serve as CEO.\n\n“It’s been an incredibly sad day for Ondo Finance,” De Bode told Cointelegraph. “Nate was not only an incredible founder and visionary, but also a very close personal friend. He will be missed dearly.”\n\n“The mission of Ondo, Nate's mission, has not changed,” he added. “If Nate were here, he would want to continue executing with excellence. We will make him proud.”\n\nOndo vice president and head of marketing, Ben Grossman, said Allman “was a once-in-a-generation founder and visionary. He was absolutely brilliant, with a vision and drive that shaped the industry and everyone around him. He will be enormously missed.”\n\nOndo did not share further details on Allman’s death. An Ondo spokesperson said that Allman’s family has requested privacy at this time.\n\nMore on the subject","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779781627981}}
{"type":"message","id":"39ce7df6","parentId":"4ab6fa2e","timestamp":"2026-05-26T07:47:11.660Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"exec_ts_ZTI0ODMwYTctNWNkNi00MmZlLTk5OGItZWU1MzllNzJiOWMz","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json\nimport os\n\ncoindesk_txt = open('/tmp/coindesk_ondo.md').read()\ncointelegraph_txt = open('/tmp/cointelegraph_ondo.md').read()\n\ncombined_text = f'COINDESK ARTICLE:\\n\\n{coindesk_txt}\\n\\nCOINTELEGRAPH ARTICLE:\\n\\n{cointelegraph_txt}'\n\ndata = {\n    'status': 'ok',\n    'story_id': 'ondo-finance-nathan-allman-passes-away-2026-05-26',\n    'topic_theme': 'Ondo Finance Founder Nathan Allman Passes Away Unexpectedly',\n    'primary_keyword': 'Nathan Allman Ondo',\n    'primary_headline': 'Ondo Finance Founder Nathan Allman Dies Unexpectedly at 32, President Ian De Bode Named CEO',\n    'primary_asset': 'Ondo Finance',\n    'chart_coin': 'ondo-finance',\n    'sources_used': ['CoinDesk', 'CoinTelegraph'],\n    'source_urls': [\n        'https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/26/ondo-finance-founder-nathan-allman-passes-away',\n        'https://cointelegraph.com/news/ondo-finance-founder-nathan-allman-passes-away-aged-32'\n    ],\n    'combined_key_facts': [\n        'Ondo Finance announced the unexpected passing of its founder, Nathan Allman, on Tuesday, May 26, 2026. He was 32 years old.',\n        'No cause of death was disclosed; Allman\\'s family has requested privacy during this difficult time.',\n        'Ian De Bode, Ondo Finance\\'s longtime president who has overseen strategy, product, and day-to-day operations for over two years, will immediately step in as CEO.',\n        'Allman was a Brown University graduate who previously worked on Goldman Sachs\\' digital assets team and founded the crypto hedge fund ChainStreet Capital.',\n        'Under Allman\\'s leadership since 2021, Ondo Finance grew into a leading pioneer of tokenized real-world assets (RWAs), reaching $3.5 billion in total value locked (TVL) with innovative products like the yield-bearing USDY stablecoin and OUSG Treasury fund.'\n    ],\n    'aggregated_raw_content': combined_text\n}\n\nos.makedirs('/tmp/crypto-run-20260526-074619/research', exist_ok=True)\nwith open('/tmp/crypto-run-20260526-074619/research/raw.json', 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n\nwith open('/tmp/researcher-raw.txt', 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(data, f, indent=2)\n\nprint('Success')\n\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":2565,"output":696,"cacheRead":13555,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":16816,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779781627982,"responseId":"_U8VaqK5Hau60r4P5radqQM"}}
